{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Rubber grommets, electrical test leads, and carbide burrs support practical workshop tasks alongside my drilling, cutting, inspection, and measurement supplies. They offer useful next steps such as protecting wiring, making test connections, and finishing drilled metal.",
    "Heavy-duty duct tape fits my repeated interest in adhesive supplies because it would help with general repairs. The rubber grommets also feel useful for a distinct purpose from my recent eyelet grommet purchase."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "RV roof tape and the radiation detector address specialized problems I have no current reason to tackle. Buying repair supplies and measurement tools does not mean I need every kind of sealant or measuring device.",
    "The replacement sprayers require compatible bottles and a need for a large quantity that my history does not establish. The clutch tension straps also lack a clear connection to a task I am doing.",
    "The metric bolt assortment fits my interests, but my recent M4–M6 kit already covers much of that need, so it is less compelling as an immediate purchase."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in workshop equipment seems to have been stretched to include specialized tools without a clear use in my recent projects.",
    "Similar product names and broad functions sometimes seem to carry too much weight: another tape needs a relevant repair purpose, and another bolt kit needs to add something beyond the sizes I recently bought."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Recent purchases matter when deciding whether I need more of something. Accessories that extend what I can do are more appealing right now than overlapping hardware assortments.",
    "Compatibility and intended use affect whether I would actually choose an item. I would check the burrs against my tools and the alcohol against my adhesive or resin work before buying.",
    "My frequent workshop purchases still serve specific tasks; they do not establish a need for bulk replacements or equipment for unrelated problems."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my practical workshop interests, but some miss the difference between a useful complement, a recent duplicate, and a specialized item without a current purpose."
}"}
